`ifndef HISI_MIPI_RX_EV200_RDL
`define HISI_MIPI_RX_EV200_RDL

regfile eHISI_MIPI_RX_EV200 {
    name = "MIPI RX / LVDS / sub-LVDS receiver (D-PHY + controller), Hi3516E V200 generation";
    desc = "
    Window 0x11240000 (0x10000), GIC SPI 45 (INTID 77); sensor clock PERI_CRG 0x120100F0 [5:2] (0x0 74.25 MHz, 0x1 72, 0x2 54, 0x3 24, 0x4 37.125, 0x5 36, 0x6 27, 0x7 12 MHz), MIPI_RX clock/reset PERI_CRG 0x120100F8, work-mode register MISC 0x12028018.
    Evidence class: **PROVEN (layout)** - register offsets, field names and bit positions are taken from the register header `mipi_rx_reg.h` of the open-source `open_mipi_rx` driver (sources/openhisilicon/kernel/mipi_rx) that OpenIPC loads on Hi3516E V200/V300 and Goke GK7205V200 boards (`#if defined(hi3516ev200)` branches select this generation: one PHY, MIPI_CTRL_INT mask 0x00030003, LVDS_CTRL_INT mask 0x0f110000). **GUESS** - access types (read-only guessed from the names _ST/_INT/STATIS/INT_RAW/TEST_OUT, everything else rw) and every reset value (the header has none, nothing is listed).
    Layout: PHY configuration block 0x000..0x1FC, system registers 0x808..0xFF8 (PHY_EN, LANE_EN, colorbar generator, interrupt), then one controller instance per sensor device (MIPI_RX_MAX_DEV_NUM = 1 for this chip: controller 0 only) with the MIPI protocol controller at 0x1004..0x12FC and the LVDS/sub-LVDS controller at 0x1300..0x1FFC.
    The register block is the same family as the Hi3516C V500 / Hi3516D V300 MIPI_RX (the same header exists under mipi_rx/hi3516cv500), not the Hi3516C V300 block of rdl/hi3516cv300 (HISI_MIPI_RX_CV300).
    ";

